All 5 tests pass consistently. Here's a summary of what was built:

## Summary

### Files Created

1. **`server.js`** — Express backend that wraps Anserini CLI commands:
   - `GET /api/health` — health check with fatjar status
   - `GET /api/catalog` — fetches inverted indexes from `PrebuiltIndexRegistry`
   - `GET /api/pairings` — derives evaluable index/topic/qrels pairings from `ReproduceFromPrebuiltIndexes` configs, filtering for BM25 conditions and adding `nDCG@10` and `Recall@1000` metrics
   - `POST /api/evaluate` — runs `SearchCollection` retrieval + `TrecEval` evaluation and returns score + metadata

2. **`public/index.html`** — Single-page dashboard with:
   - Searchable index catalog (109 inverted indexes, 27 evaluable)
   - EVALUABLE vs CATALOG badges to distinguish indexes
   - Topic/qrels pairing selector
   - Metric selector with nDCG@10, Recall@1000, MAP, etc.
   - Run Evaluation button with progress state
   - Score display + full run metadata (index, topics, metric, timing, file paths, evaluation output)

3. **`tests/e2e.spec.js`** — Playwright e2e test (5 tests):
   - CACM selected by default with correct pairing
   - Catalog exposes more than CACM (109 indexes total)
   - nDCG@10 evaluation returns numeric score (0.4543)
   - Recall@1000 evaluation returns numeric score (0.8867)
   - Catalog-only indexes visible but not selectable for evaluation

4. **`playwright.config.js`** — Playwright configuration

### Key Design Decisions
- Uses real Anserini CLI registry discovery (no hardcoded catalogs)
- Pairings derived from `ReproduceFromPrebuiltIndexes` YAML configs
- Only BM25 conditions included (matching server capabilities)
- nDCG@10 and Recall@1000 added as universally-available metrics
- CACM defaults as the selected evaluable index